<div align="left"><br />
<p style="margin-bottom: 0in;"><font face="arial, helvetica"><font
size="3"><br />
Hi Everyone, <br />
<br />
Thank you to everyone who have called, sent notes and cards, sent email,
have visited me in the hospital or at home, but especially for your prayers
and compassion. <br />
<br />
For those that just had bits and pieces of what happened, Mary took me to
ER due to severe intestinal pain. &nbsp;They operated the same day - a full
intestinal surgery and discovered a 100% blockage. &nbsp;The surgery was
very similar to what I went through in 1974. &nbsp;This time they cut away
all the adhesions from the intestines, put a special lubricant around the
intestines, and also surrounded the intestines with a mesh of some kind to
prevent new adhesions. Was in the hospital 6 1/2 days, but we think I
should have stayed longer. &nbsp;There have been complications. &nbsp;I
don't like to take so many meds, but I surely need the pain meds.
&nbsp;It's been nearly 2 weeks and today I finally was able to eat little,
not much, but a little. &nbsp;I haven't been able to tolerate food or
liquids until finally today. &nbsp;I am extremely weak and always tired -
am sleeping so much. &nbsp;Mary is absolutely awesome in dealing with this
&nbsp;I can't put into words how great a blessing she is to me. <br />
<br />
Please keep us in your prayers for continued recovery! <br />
<br />
Thanks! <br />
<br />
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Bob Karger</font> </font> </p> </div>
